Subject: [PATCH 08117/11362] [outer-loop] Correct the inert-defer action
 ledger: the only action "saving" is one game collapsing

Adversarial review of 09ec7f26ab found the `actions` row misleading. Verified against
the run's own cells before applying; all corrections are additive.

* NO action saving was measured, and none could be. 75/75 control cells are budget-bound
  at 2000. The corpus-wide reduction is 50000 -> 49022 = 978 actions, and g50t alone is
  -978: 100% of it. g50t is the arm's worst regression -- frontier exhausted at 1022
  actions (timed_out=false) with states 142 -> 56 and hv 0.6667 -> 0.3333. It is also the
  largest `nav` improvement. Both rows are now marked uninformative.
* Where the freed actions went (new decomposition, per roster pass): inert -4969, but
  probe_moved_the_board +2234, walk_or_replay +1281, reset_action +476 -- 3991 of 4969
  (80.3%) re-spent in the same budget. That is why a 54% class cut moves totals by 2%.
* `hv flat` was the pooled reading and is retracted: 1 better / 1 worse, but -50.0% vs
  +9.1%.
* cd82 loses a level at k=4 as at k=1, but k=4 is NET NEUTRAL on levels (m0r0 gains one).
* The task premise's score conversion (-19.13% actions -> 1.53x) is retracted: it needs
  the trajectory to shorten. The artifact never asserted it. `per_level_score_conversion`
  is a different, still-valid quantity.

Two claims strengthened rather than corrected:
* Solve-conditioning audited explicitly. No get_adapter call site in the live path;
  build_progress_window never called; 250/250 cells start_level=0 with one bootstrap.reset;
  0 plan.execute_step. The one identity-keyed input that DOES reach the run is the
  registry `mechanic_class` (sb26, tn36 -> explore_budget 24; the other 23 get the
  hidden-game default 80). Load-bearing on exactly one game: forcing 80 on sb26 diverges
  the trace (states 769 -> 714); tn36 and cd82 counterfactuals are byte-identical. Cannot
  bias the A/B -- both arms get the same value -- so it is a hidden-game transfer caveat,
  which is why solve_provenance is development_proxy.
* The 3 -> 6 live-budget headline is NOT a truncation artifact. Re-ran ft09/lp85/su15
  natively at --budget 400: control banks 0 on all three, defer banks 1 on each, and
  actions-to-first-levelup matches the truncated reading exactly (256/154/300).

Recommendation unchanged and better supported: do not flip the default.

